<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ulster Bank launches EMU guide for Irish business.</title>
<headline>Ulster Bank launches EMU guide for Irish business.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ulster Bank, the Irish arm of National Westminster Bank Plc, on Thursday launched a new guide for Irish business on preparing for economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;Companies need to undertake a great deal of research and planning if they are to devise a changeover strategy that is best suited to their needs and the competitive market in which they operate,&quot; Pat McArdle, head of the strategic and economic planning unit at Ulster Bank, said.</p>
<p>The guide will be distributed to customers over coming weeks and will be updated with additional sections as the start date for EMU draws closer, a statement from Ulster Bank said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
